## Risk Considerations

This tool is **read-only**: it never modifies, deletes, or disables
anything in Splunk. It only reads metadata (ingest volume and usage
signals) — see docs/security.md.

These figures are estimates based on Splunk metadata (ingest volume and
search/alert/dashboard activity), **not a financial audit**.

Datasets classified as `PROTECTED` were deliberately excluded from
optimization candidates, regardless of their usage signals.

Datasets classified as `UNKNOWN` are excluded from the savings calculation —
we could not determine their usage with high confidence, so we do not guess.

{% if show_squashing_note %}
This report analyzes usage at the (index, sourcetype) level only. Splunk's
license usage reporting can "squash" host and source breakdowns in
high-cardinality environments — see Methodology.
{% endif %}

**No action should be taken without manual validation by a Splunk
administrator and the team that owns each dataset.**

